  "title": "Sciencetasia",
  "description": "Take a musical journey to the International Space Station, where amazing science awaits.   This is Sciencetasia! Astronaut Woody Hoburg introduces you to a swirling, colorful and mesmerizing collection of real science experiments conducted in space…all set to classical music!   You will see…  Plant growth experiments! Astronaut Christina Koch helps you discover how NASA’s garden grows in space. Watch out for the hot peppers! (Set to the \"Waltz of the Flowers\" by Tchaikovsky)  Combustion Science! “The science of fire.”  Astronaut Mark Vande Hei explores how NASA studies bouncing, dancing, pulsing flames in space.   (Set to Symphony No 6 In F Major Op 68 (Pastoral) by Beethoven)  Fluid experiments!  Astronaut Megan McArthur introduces you to the shapeshifting world of fluids and the fascinating ways they behave onboard the space station.  (Set to “La Mer” by Debussy)  More information on this “symphony of science” can be found at www.nasa.gov/iss-science",
  "keywords": "International Space Station, Science, Sciencetasia, microgravity, microgravity science, combustion science, plant growth experiments, fluid science",
